From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:13:47 +0800
Subject: power: supply: piano_mca: share standard thermal charge limits

Expose charge_control_limit and a thermal cooling device with
descending DT-supplied current limits. Use one total battery-current
budget for the pump and PMIC. A budget below the pump's minimum
keeps charging on the PMIC. Zero current pauses battery charging
while external power remains available.

Retire the active pump before tightening current. Stop and reopen
it after a budget increase so source and protection limits can be
recalculated. Preserve failed restrictions for retry and preserve
completed tail charging and hardware fault stops. Clear stale
permission at the start of every new stop and allow restart only
after a confirmed temperature or limit stop.

Retain cooling requests issued during registration. The first
GLINK service notification applies that request. Serialize updates
with policy work, suspend and teardown. Keep the limits across
ADSP restarts and cable changes, and use the normal temperature
and source checks when restoring charging.

Signed-off-by: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
